# Input/output PII/jailbreak/off-topic checks are handled by the built-in
# "self check input" / "self check output" flows (see guardrails/config.yml,
# section `rails:` + custom prompts under `prompts:`). Those flows call the
# self_check_input / self_check_output actions, which ask the LLM a direct
# Yes/No policy-violation question — this is the pattern NeMo Guardrails
# actually supports for `rails.input.flows` / `rails.output.flows`.
#
# No "define user ..." canonical forms here on purpose: declaring one makes
# NeMo build a sentence-embedding index for intent matching at startup, which
# needs its own model download and isn't needed by the LLM-prompt-based
# self-check flows above.

define flow self check facts
  $facts = execute check_facts
  if not $facts.accurate
    bot say "Lưu ý: Câu trả lời trên có thể không chính xác. Vui lòng xác nhận với phòng Nhân sự."
